{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "nr-commercial-nation",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7e: the `nr-commercial-nation` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE -- the whole nation, August 2020, weekday, the Commercial sector, gasoline, THC, CO, NOx and PM10: 52 equipment points over ten 2- and 4-stroke SCCs, 227 cohorts, 908 rows. The first NATION-level run.\n\nA NATION RUN IS ONE RUN AT A STATE MOVES FOLDS, not a sum of state runs. `PreAggNATION.sql` rewrites the population, growth pattern, month allocation, zone temperature and fuel supply as state 0 before NONROAD reads them, and each fold was measured against this run's execution database before it was ported -- the population's 1,183 rows at 7e-16, the growth pattern's 246 of 246, the month's 840 of 840, the 24 hourly temperatures at 4e-13, the 45 formulations' shares at the 3.6e-7 of their f32 column. All 908 rows then reproduced on the model's first run, at 6.729e-06.\n\nTWO OF THE FOLDS IT CANNOT SEE. Each of its ten SCCs has one growth-pattern row, so the minimum over states is that row; and its August month fraction is 1/12, which is also the model's fallback. A probe of `nr-lawn-garden-county`'s SCCs at the nation checked both instead -- 97 points on SCCs whose pattern differs by state, and month fractions of 0 to 0.137 -- against a pandas replica of `PreAggNATION.sql`: no mismatch. `nr-railroad-support-nation`'s oracle covers both."
  },
  "domain": {
    "element_type": "Float32"
  },
